{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":373,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This entry includes the baseplate wedge 1 protein of bacteriophage PhiTE that infects the plant pathogen Pectobacterium atrosepticum. Wedge 1 is a component of the wedge complex that comprises six lobed protomeric units in the baseplate. Each protomer contains a single copy of wedge 1 protein, two copies of wedge 2 protein in alternate conformations, and a singular IG-like protein referred to as the spacer. Wedge 1 forms the bulk of the wedge structure along with wedge 2, constituting the canonical trifurcation unit that acts as a coordination platform adhering wedge 1 and 2 proteins into a continuous ring. The short tail fiber (STF) attaches to wedge 1 monomers through its N-terminal loops that form a globular joint, making electrostatic and hydrophobic interactions. Wedge 1 also forms a putative disulfide bond with the sheath initiator (SI) protein (Wedge1:C143, SI:C143) that may serve as a pivoting point to transduce signals associated with receptor binding.","domain_architectures":10,"interpro_id":"IPR021283","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":886,"name":"Bacteriophage baseplate wedge 1 protein","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF11041","proteins":835,"proteomes":694,"short_name":"Phage_Wedge1","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF11041","structures":10,"taxa":1468,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF11041.yaml","record":